<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmed Muhtar Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1839–1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Gazi Ahmed Muhtar Pasha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmed Muhtar Pasha was an Ottoman general and statesman. In 1872 he led the expedition that took Sanaa and established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilayet">Vilayet</a>, and he became a hero for his defence of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1877-1878">Russo-Turkish War</a> of 1877 to 1878, earning the title Gazi. He served briefly as grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> in 1912.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmed-muhtar-pasha.jpg" alt="Ahmed Muhtar Pasha" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al1-5235-6C52-7E70.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
